{#- The page, minified and DEFLATE-compressed by render.py, carried as base64 in this one
    script. Unpacking is the browser's own DecompressionStream, which every Chromium with
    WebHID has had since before the page needed it. 'deflate' is the zlib format that
    zlib.compress() writes, header and checksum included, so the browser verifies what it
    unpacked. The promise settles after this outer document has finished loading, so
    document.open() replaces it rather than appending to it, and the written page fires a
    load event of its own. Anything driving the page from outside has to wait for that
    second document to be ready, as misc/test-config-page.py does. -#}
<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><script>{% raw %}new Response(new Blob([Uint8Array.from(atob('{% endraw %}{{payload}}{% raw %}'),c=>c.charCodeAt(0))]).stream().pipeThrough(new DecompressionStream('deflate'))).text().then(t=>{document.open();document.write(t);document.close()}){% endraw %}</script></head><body></body></html>
